From b9efb093be239549e1e315aa02f20483f23aa404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Cain <brian.cain@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:46:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] h2: vmwork: keep VMWORK set while guest interrupts are
 disabled

06e67bbb (VMOP_KILL_THREAD) made H2K_vm_do_work_withlock clear VMWORK
unconditionally.  Before it, the bit was cleared only when the guest had
interrupts enabled.

With that change, a Linux guest on the qcs6490-cdsp QEMU machine mostly
stops booting with four VCPUs: the kernel prints nothing, loadlinux
reports "linux: booted", and every hardware thread ends up idle in
H2K_wait_forever.  With one or two VCPUs it still boots.  In twelve boots
the build with 06e67bbb reached the Linux console 0 times; the same build
with the guard below restored did so 12 times.  Builds without 06e67bbb
boot every time.

Restore the IE guard.  The KILL check at the top of the function still
runs first and never returns, so the killed-thread escape that 06e67bbb
fixed stays fixed.

The futex, popup and intpool blocking primitives gate on VMWORK alone
since 06e67bbb, so while a thread runs with interrupts disabled and
something pending they fail and the caller retries, where before
06e67bbb they would have blocked.  The vmwork unit test case that asserted
VMWORK is cleared on the IE-disabled path is updated to expect it set.

Signed-off-by: Brian Cain <brian.cain@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 kernel/vm/vmwork/test/test.c  |  2 +-
 kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.ref.c |  8 +++++++-
 kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.spec  | 14 +++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/vm/vmwork/test/test.c b/kernel/vm/vmwork/test/test.c
index 22796c91..eacd5b0c 100644
--- a/kernel/vm/vmwork/test/test.c
+++ b/kernel/vm/vmwork/test/test.c
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ int main()
 	if (TH_saw_interrupt_get) FAIL("Saw interrupt get while !IE");
 	if (!TH_saw_interrupt_peek) FAIL("Didn't see interrupt peek while !IE");
 	if (TH_saw_vm_event) FAIL("Did a VM event");
-	if (a.vmstatus & H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK) FAIL("VMWORK not cleared (no IE)");
+	if (!(a.vmstatus & H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK)) FAIL("VMWORK cleared while !IE");
 	TH_saw_thread_stop = TH_saw_vm_event = TH_saw_interrupt_get = TH_saw_interrupt_peek = 0;
 
 	a.vmstatus = H2K_VMSTATUS_IE | H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK;
diff --git a/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.ref.c b/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.ref.c
index 05d824ae..eec16331 100644
--- a/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.ref.c
+++ b/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.ref.c
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@ s32_t H2K_vm_do_work_withlock(H2K_thread_context *me)
 
 	if (!(me->vmstatus & H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK)) return -1;
 
-	H2K_atomic_clrbit(&me->atomic_status_word,H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK_BIT);
+	/*
+	 * With guest interrupts disabled, leave VMWORK set: the guest may go to
+	 * vmwait before it re-enables them.
+	 */
+	if (me->vmstatus & H2K_VMSTATUS_IE) {
+		H2K_atomic_clrbit(&me->atomic_status_word,H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK_BIT);
+	}
 	return H2K_vm_check_interrupts(me);
 }
diff --git a/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.spec b/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.spec
index 13402ba5..6e73f0cc 100644
--- a/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.spec
+++ b/kernel/vm/vmwork/vmwork.spec
@@ -19,8 +19,12 @@ the normal kill path does not return.  Otherwise, if the
 ``H2K_VMSTATUS_VMWORK`` bit is clear, returns ``-1`` without changing the
 context.
 
-When VMWORK is set, atomically clears the VMWORK bit and calls
-:c:func:`H2K_vm_check_interrupts()`.  That check either consumes and raises a
-pending interrupt when guest interrupts are enabled, or only observes a
-pending interrupt when they are disabled.  The result of that check is returned
-to the caller.
+When VMWORK is set and guest interrupts are enabled (``H2K_VMSTATUS_IE``),
+atomically clears the VMWORK bit and calls
+:c:func:`H2K_vm_check_interrupts()`, which consumes and raises a pending
+interrupt.  When guest interrupts are disabled, the VMWORK bit is left set,
+because the guest may go to ``vmwait`` before it re-enables them; the check
+then only observes a pending interrupt.  Either way, the result of
+:c:func:`H2K_vm_check_interrupts()` is returned to the caller.  A block
+primitive that gates on VMWORK therefore fails and is retried while the guest
+runs with interrupts disabled and something pending.
\ No newline at end of file
